    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21358" root="سوى" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِوَآءٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِىٌّ</span>, second sentence, in two places:
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَوَآءٌ</span> also, in the latter half of the paragraph:
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِوًى</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَعَثُوا بِالسِّوَآءِ وَاللِّوَآءِ</span> means
(assumed tropical:)  <i>They sent seeking,</i> or <i>demanding, aid,</i> or <i>succour.</i>
(K in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لوى</span>. [The proper signification of
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السِّوَآء</span> in this instance I do not find explained.])

